# BUGS

A native program's call is flushed by a note only if its connection's `interrupted` hook says so; without one, a read a server holds waits until it is answered.

Before `Tversion` a `Tflush` is answered with an `Rerror`, `fid already in use`, as every request is there; 9P2000 has no `Rerror` for a `Tflush`.
